#### PRE-REGISTERED per-cell predictions for sweep A ####
Written at 2026-09-03T03:11:11+08:00, while cell r2M was still running and cells r1M..r60k had not started.
Only green20M and r5M had been read at this point (both 30/30 on all three windows).

Calibration, measured not assumed: the proxy's own send-side counter
  (GET :8081/sflow/stats) moved 1403->2478 = 1075 datagrams in the 58 s of the 20 Mbit/s
  cell = 18.5 samples/s, and 2478->2751 = 273 in 58 s of the 5 Mbit/s cell = 4.7/s.
  Model 3*R/(8*1400*256) predicts 20.9/s and 5.2/s. So the flow TABLE is refreshed by
  lambda = 3R/2867200 per second (3 sampling hops: s1, s5, s2 -- from the row's own path).
  One EDGE (window A at dpid 5) sees lambda/3.

Sampling is Bernoulli, not a counter: ndtwin_switch.p4:405 is
  random(meta.sample_rand, 0, SAMPLE_RATE-1); if (meta.sample_rand == 0) clone.
  So inter-sample gaps are exponential and P(a poll finds age < W) = 1 - exp(-lambda*W).

